  "correspondence": "For arbitrary finite families of nonnegative degrees a_i,b_j, original sheaf polynomial matrices between varied twists T(-a_i-r-1) and T(-b_j-r-1) induce the actual matrix of homogeneous multiplication transposes on native top Cech homology. Negative multiplying degrees have proved zero entries. Actual sheaf/complex degree transports, biproduct preservation and cokernel quotient compatibility are verified. This is the varied free-twist matrix case, not cohomology of a coherent sheaf presentation; that affine exactness/top-Cech cokernel bridge, derived comparison, Koszul restriction and original4.1/4.2 remain OPEN.",
